{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1143205-m20-question","id":1143205,"title":"M20 Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-23T05:26:28-07:00","id":1143205,"title":"M20 Question","content":"Ok, so I know in older additions you could get away with using a vulgar effect as coincidental if another supernatural did it first. Is that still a thing in M20, and if so anyone know where it would be mentioned (the M20 book is very big and I'm not really looking forward to digging through it if I can help it)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13838-hangedman1984","name":"hangedman1984","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13838_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T09:52:12-07:00","id":1143257,"title":"","content":"As far as I know there has never been anything like that in Ascension. Vulgar is vulgar, full stop.<br /> There might be conditions that make specific Vulgar magic coincidental (and vice-versa), but it's definitely not something that can be caused by people casting fireballs before of you. I actually remember the manuals saying instead that even coincidental effects can become vulgar if they're reiterated often enough in a short timeframe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T10:22:44-07:00","id":1143268,"title":"","content":"For the first question, look at Reality Zones. In Reality Zones, vulgar is different based on the beliefs of others. Sanctum allows the user's paradigm to be coincidental in the Sanctum, which might allow coincidental magical use by another supernatural if they share the paradigm. Keep in mind that only mages have to worry about Paradox--werewolves and vampires and other supernaturals use different magic rules.<br /> <br /> The Domino Effect is the rule about where repeated magic that was coincidental becomes vulgar. Think of this as doing something improbable too many times. For example, an amateur golfer scores a bunch of holes in one at a tough golf course such as St. Andrews in Scotland. Another example would be consistently picking winning lottery numbers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T11:58:01-07:00","id":1143290,"title":"","content":"I'm guessing the question is more along the lines of &quot;If my Verbena uses Life to grow fangs and then I suck blood out of someone and use that as an excuse to heal myself, is that vulgar or coincidental, since the mage looks exactly like a vampire and they aren't vulgar&quot; and I think the answer is.... No? Probably not? Almost certainly not? <br /> <br /> I certainly don't remember it in M20. <br /> <br /> Sounds like something that some Hollow Ones might try and, in the right Reality Zone, like, say, the Succubus Club, might work....<br /> <br /> (I picked vampires deliberately, since they are the supernatural without Veil, Mists, etc. that mostly protects from human interaction, meaning humans don't really believe in what they are and can do since they really can't believe in something that is beyond the possibility of their belief.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T14:56:14-07:00","id":1143332,"title":"","content":"I don't remember if 1e said something to that extent, but everything from 2e on has said that Mages can't copy other supernaturals to avoid their magic being vulgar.<br /> <br /> That there's no way to take advantage of other supernaturals to make magic easier. It's just never going to come down to &quot;a Tremere threw a fireball with Lure of Flames, so I can do so coincidentally.&quot; As noted, supernaturals can create small local Reality Zones that might let appropriate magic be coincidental there (A mage that's allowed into the Bawn of a Sept and has a shamanistic Focus could probably follow Gaian cosmological principles for coincidental magic there like a Sanctum does). Blatancy rolls might be possible/easier if other supernaturals are running around doing crazy stuff. Something M20 introduced in a more codified fashion is pulling on mystic threads, so copying supernatural powers might not make magic coincidental but it would reduce the difficulty of the effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T21:07:36-07:00","id":1145972,"title":"","content":"Perhaps what you're thinking of is that other Supernaturals typically don't count as Sleeper witnesses for Vulgar effects? If you're surrounded by Vampires and nothing else a fireball spell or body tearing spell will be considered Vulgar Without Witnesses for the difficulty modifier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T10:23:44-07:00","id":1146373,"title":"","content":"Given that vulgar is only 1 paradox for either flavor unless you botch in Mage 20, the real difference between going vulgar without witnesses and going vulgar with witnesses will be the difficulty.<br /> <br /> Gifts are explained in M20 Book of Secrets as being different from Spheres (page 271) and there is a reference back to Mage 20 (page 546) on Nightfolk countermagic. That being said, rituals practiced by another supernatural group might inspire a Mage's rituals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}